      fix: parse TS 5.0 type-only star re-exports in typescript/tsx grammars
      
      The pinned tree-sitter-typescript grammar (75b3874) rejects
      `export type * from "…"` and `export type * as ns from "…"`,
      producing an ERROR node at the `type` token and abandoning the rest
      of the file (semgrep/semgrep#11871; upstream
      tree-sitter/tree-sitter-typescript#348 still open).
      
      Extend the semgrep wrapper grammars' `export_statement` with the two
      star forms, wrapping `previous` so the existing CST variant names stay
      stable (node-types.json is byte-identical before/after). Add a corpus
      regression test.
      
      The generated parsers under languages/typescript/tree-sitter/ still
      need `make regen-grammar-typescript && make regen-grammar-tsx`
      (full toolchain with ocaml-tree-sitter) before merge.
      
      Assisted-by: Muse AI agent (T138)
